    "q-129799": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129799",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Compute the Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ for ${y}_{1}(x)=2{e}^{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{2x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ of two functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nW({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & {y}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}|={y}_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}-{y}_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have ${y}_{1}(x)=2{e}^{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{2x}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({y}_{1},{y}_{2}) & =(2{e}^{x}){({e}^{2x})}^{′}-({e}^{2x}){(2{e}^{x})}^{′} \\\\  & =(2{e}^{x})(2{e}^{2x})-({e}^{2x})(2{e}^{x}) \\\\  & ={4}^{3x}-2{e}^{3x} \\\\  & =2{e}^{3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-129799-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "2{e}^{3x}",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"18\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-msup><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D452 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.363em;\"><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msup></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
